second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is the artist of the album \\\"Lazy Afternoon\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"artist\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 123, \"text\": \"A Lazy Afternoon (Harold Land album) A Lazy Afternoon is a studio album by American hard bop tenor saxophonist Harold Land.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d00\", \"start\": 124, \"end\": 209, \"text\": \"The album was recorded in Hollywood and released in 1995 via Postcards Records label.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d00\", \"start\": 210, \"end\": 369, \"text\": \"Scott Yanow of Allmusic wrote \\\"Harold Land, a long underrated tenor giant based in Los Angeles, is quite melodic yet subtly explorative on his surprising disc.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d00\", \"start\": 370, \"end\": 589, \"text\": \"Backed by a string orchestra arranged and conducted by Ray Ellis and a rhythm section led by pianist Bill Henderson, Land explores dozen standards that are highlighted by \\\"Nature Boy,\\\" \\\"Invitation\\\" and \\\"You've Changed.\\\"\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d00\", \"start\": 590, \"end\": 617, \"text\": \"He treats the melodies with\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 118, \"text\": \"Lazy Afternoon (Barbra Streisand album) Lazy Afternoon is a studio album recorded by American singer Barbra Streisand.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01\", \"start\": 119, \"end\": 175, \"text\": \"It was released on October 14, 1975 by Columbia Records.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01\", \"start\": 176, \"end\": 399, \"text\": \"After releasing the \\\"Funny Lady\\\" soundtrack earlier in 1975, the singer began working with new musicians for the project following the mediocre critical response generated from her previous studio album, \\\"ButterFly\\\" (1974).\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01\", \"start\": 400, \"end\": 479, \"text\": \"Recorded in April 1975 in Los Angeles, \\\"Lazy Afternoon\\\" contains pop standards.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01\", \"start\": 480, \"end\": 612, \"text\": \"Producer Rupert Holmes wrote four songs on the album, and Streisand received her first songwriting credit for the song \\\"By the Way\\\".\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01\", \"start\": 613, \"end\": 649, \"text\": \"She also included a few cover songs,\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"artist\", \"scope\": \"album \\\"Lazy Afternoon\\\"\", \"claim\": \"Harold Land is the artist of the album \\\"Lazy Afternoon\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Harold Land\", \"quote\": \"A Lazy Afternoon (Harold Land album) A Lazy Afternoon is a studio album by American hard bop tenor saxophonist Harold Land.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0103-27e854bd1855:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"artist\", \"scope\": \"album \\\"Lazy Afternoon\\\"\", \"claim\": \"Barbra Streisand is the artist of the album \\\"Lazy Afternoon\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Barbra Streisand\", \"quote\": \"Lazy Afternoon (Barbra Streisand album) Lazy Afternoon is a studio album recorded by American singer Barbra Streisand.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Harold 